# M1 / B010 — add-dependency, angular, api-versioning, architecture-decision.

C R142 OL DEP-002 | MUST NOT | Use the approved technology when one exists (technology stack and capability decisions) rather than silently selecting an alternative; replacing an approved technology is Reserved. | technology choices | Approved replacement.
C R143 OL DEP-017 | DEFAULT | Add a versioning package only after the project has explicitly adopted Controller API versioning; then use the Controller integration of Asp.Versioning (Asp.Versioning.Mvc, plus Asp.Versioning.Mvc.ApiExplorer). | API versioning packages | none stated
C R144 OL DEP-004 | MUST | Before installing check whether the selected package/version is deprecated, known vulnerability information and the license of the exact version from official registry metadata (and upstream when necessary); downloadable without payment does not mean acceptable; check manifests and vulnerability information when verifying the dependency. | dependency additions and updates | none stated
C R145 OL DEP-005 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD) may be accepted; do not install automatically a paid/commercial dependency or one with material obligations or unclassifiable licensing; explain the concern and present alternatives (say so when none exists) without silently substituting; no legal conclusions beyond the published license. | dependency additions | User decision.
C R147 OL GOV-014 | MUST | Keep changes focused on the requested scope and preserve existing behavior unless the task or approved specification requires a change (e.g. do not automatically replace or upgrade unrelated packages after a scanner finding; no unrelated dependency cleanup in narrow tasks). | all changes | Task or approved specification requires change.
C R148 OL GOV-012 | DEFAULT | Prefer simple, maintainable solutions and avoid speculative abstractions (e.g. no custom abstraction around every UI-library component without a concrete reason). | all code | none stated
C R149 OL WF-016 | DEFAULT | Treat generated code as generated: keep it separate from handwritten logic and regenerate it when the source contract changes; fix wrong generated output at its source. | generated code | none stated
C R150 OL DEP-014 | DECIDED | Frontend baseline: latest stable Angular supported by the selected Node.js environment, created with the current Angular CLI, which selects mutually compatible TypeScript and RxJS versions (TypeScript not upgraded beyond Angular's supported range); standalone APIs, strict mode, routing, zoneless change detection when supported, SCSS, Angular Material and CDK, Vitest. | frontend workspace | none stated
C R151 OL DEP-024,DEP-013 | DEFAULT | Keep backend production and test projects (backend/<Name>.<Layer>/), the frontend workspace (frontend/<Name>.Web/, with unit/component tests colocated and E2E under e2e/) and documentation separated per the repository layout; backend test projects live under backend/ beside the production projects; no separate top-level tests/ directory. | repository layout | none stated
C R152 OL WF-018 | MUST | Build and test the frontend through the scripts the workspace actually defines; never invent npm scripts; in CI use npm ci when a maintained lockfile supports it. | frontend commands and CI | none stated
C R153 OL GOV-017 | MUST | Classify every consequential choice: Decided (settled by these instructions, decision records, the approved specification, established structure or an accepted ADR; do not reopen without approval), Delegated (local, reversible, no material boundary, dependency, convention, contract or behavior change; decide yourself), Reserved (explicit approval); an explicit user instruction counts as approval. | all consequential choices | none stated
C R154 OL GOV-017 | MUST | Raise a Reserved decision as a Decision Request (Context, Options, Recommendation, Blocked, Proceeding with) through architecture-decision and wait for an explicit answer before implementing the Reserved part. | Reserved decisions | none stated
C R155 OL GOV-017 | MUST | In an autonomous or headless run continue only on the policy-compliant non-Reserved path named in 'Proceeding with', never make a Reserved decision silently, and list every unresolved Decision Request in the final report. | headless runs | none stated
C R156 OL GOV-007 | MUST | When a new behavioral rule is approved, update the durable source of truth in the same change, including SPECIFICATION.md when appropriate. | approved product behavior | none stated
C R157 OL GOV-008 | MUST | CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md holds approved project-level tunable product limits and defaults (maximum lengths, page sizes, retention periods, numeric thresholds); SPECIFICATION.md owns behavioral intent; tunable values are recorded through custom-settings. | product settings | none stated
C R158 OL GOV-006 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Observable string semantics (case sensitivity, collation, culture vs ordinal, normalization, trimming, uniqueness, lookup) are product behavior; when approved sources do not define them and the choice affects equality, uniqueness, lookup or accepted input, ask for approval instead of choosing silently; the persistence collation default is a technology default, and changing effective string comparison (e.g. through a declared-property change) is a product decision that must not happen silently. | product behavior | none stated
C X16 EX DEP-001,GOV-014 | MUST | Remove dependencies that are no longer used when that is part of the current change and safe to verify; do not leave dead package references. | dependency changes | Unrelated cleanup during a narrowly scoped task is excluded. | DEP-001 restricts additions and GOV-014 limits scope; no oracle policy requires removing dependencies made unused by a change. | A refactor that stops using a package must also remove its reference.
C X17 EX GOV-017,GOV-007 | MUST | Accepted architecture, stack, convention or public-contract decisions are recorded in the same change as an ADR in docs/decisions/NNNN-short-title.md (Status, Context, Decision, Consequences) and in the affected decision record (technology stack or capability planning facet); a rejected request is recorded only when the rejection itself is a durable decision. | approved decisions | Product behavior and tunable values go to SPECIFICATION.md / CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md. | GOV-017 requires approval for Reserved decisions but no recording artifact; no oracle policy requires ADRs or decision-record updates. | After approval to add a new library, the change is incomplete until the ADR and the stack record are written.
C X18 EX ARC-020,GOV-017,DEP-002 | MUST | Changing a capability selection, enabling or disabling the optional frontend slot, or changing a declared property such as the persistence provider variant is Reserved and requires an ADR; after approval the replacement itself is applied by the user-run template-maintenance workflow (Capability Replacement). | capability selection changes | none stated | ARC-020/DEP-002 require approval for replacing approved technology, but no oracle policy requires an ADR or routes the change through a user-run maintenance workflow. | After the user approves switching the test framework, the agent records the ADR and asks the user to run /template-maintenance instead of editing the modules itself.

